{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJp2VMNszpzgXYrfLjSPGL","type":"tool_result","content":"# Versioned browser libraries\n\nThis shelf lets imported games retain their requested engine version and\nrenderer. It is separate from the patched shared stack at `/lib/three/`,\n`/lib/rapier/` and `/lib/kit/`; existing games keep using those paths.\n\n## Available releases\n\nThree.js includes **every stable release and patch** in the requested range:\n\n`0.180.0`, `0.181.0`, `0.181.1`, `0.181.2`, `0.182.0`, `0.183.0`, `0.183.1`,\n`0.183.2`, `0.184.0`, `0.185.0`, `0.185.1`, `0.186.0`, `0.186.1`.\n\nEach is the full official npm package: classic WebGL and WebGPU builds, TSL,\nall addons, source modules, fonts, Draco and Basis decoders, and the license.\nThe versioned packages are upstream distributions, without the shared stack's\nlocal patches or WebGL-only exclusions.\n\nThe shelf also pins **Three.js 0.160.0** and older **Rapier 3D compat** releases:\n**0.14.0** for The Ash-Bound Prophecy and **0.19.0** for Ashbound: The Sleeper’s\nOath. These are full official packages, preserved on every sync so the games\nretain their original WebGL renderer and physics.\nThe r160 browser fixture exercises classic WebGL and addons; newer releases\nalso exercise the modern WebGPU build and TSL.\n\nRapier includes **0.19.3, 0.20.0 and 0.21.0** for all 12 official packages:\n\n| Dimension | Standard | SIMD | Deterministic |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2D | `rapier2d`, `rapier2d-compat` | `rapier2d-simd`, `rapier2d-simd-compat` | `rapier2d-deterministic`, `rapier2d-deterministic-compat` |\n| 3D | `rapier3d`, `rapier3d-compat` | `rapier3d-simd`, `rapier3d-simd-compat` | `rapier3d-deterministic`, `rapier3d-deterministic-compat` |\n\nAll package names have the `@dimforge/` scope. Stable releases are included;\nnightly/canary builds are outside this shelf. The starting version `0.193`\nwas interpreted as the published release `0.19.3`.\n\n## Importing games\n\nUse `pnpm ingest <file|folder|zip>`. The importer rewrites recognized Three.js\nand Rapier URLs in HTML, JavaScript and CSS to local paths. Supported hosts:\njsDelivr (npm and Three.js GitHub tags), unpkg, esm.sh, Skypack, JSPM, cdnjs,\nand the official Three.js build/examples paths.\n\nExact version pins stay exact. Partial versions and `^0.x`/`~0.x` ranges select\na compatible local patch. Unmapped bare imports use the detected package\nversion, or the latest version in `manifest.json` when none is specified;\nunversioned CDN references also use the latest. The importer adds per-version\nimport-map scopes so addons and TSL resolve their own version of Three.js.\nExisting mappings, game assets, embedded bundles and game logic are retained.\nThe dry-run report lists dependencies that would become local. Re-importing\nthe same input still skips it as a duplicate.\n\nUnavailable releases and files are reported and left unchanged. A URL for an\nold global `three.min.js` build is not silently replaced by an ES module:\nthose global builds are not part of r180 onward. Arbitrary missing game files,\nother libraries, custom CDN-generated bundles, or incompatible game code still\nneed individual attention. Installing engines cannot supply missing models,\ntextures, levels or audio.\n\n## Manual paths\n=====\n37:| `<meta name=\"description\">` | The blurb in the drawer |\n38:| `<meta name=\"theme-color\">` | That cabinet's marquee colour and the light it throws |\n40:| `<meta property=\"og:image\">` | Its cover art, in a project folder that ships the image |\n164:  folder. A zip of several single-file games becomes a collection. A package\n216:**Size.** GitHub refuses any single file over 100 MB and warns above 50 MB;\n358:The hub as a console's home screen, for a TV and a controller. One game at a\n368:| | Keyboard | Controller |\n389:random games, like a console's attract mode.\n489:In short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\n592:After the picks, **Random Mode** deals. The hub deals every game that declares `hub:session` and\n623:  the browser, as `localStorage['ai-hub:relay-only']`).\n624:- While no game in the library declares `hub:session`, the reference games\n734:own, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\n741:an override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n757:checks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n758:(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9652e092-8cd1-4acd-9328-de6431071aa9","uuid":"bc805fe3-7b34-481d-b22c-78428bc427c6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:57.870Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Versioned browser libraries\n\nThis shelf lets imported games retain their requested engine version and\nrenderer. It is separate from the patched shared stack at `/lib/three/`,\n`/lib/rapier/` and `/lib/kit/`; existing games keep using those paths.\n\n## Available releases\n\nThree.js includes **every stable release and patch** in the requested range:\n\n`0.180.0`, `0.181.0`, `0.181.1`, `0.181.2`, `0.182.0`, `0.183.0`, `0.183.1`,\n`0.183.2`, `0.184.0`, `0.185.0`, `0.185.1`, `0.186.0`, `0.186.1`.\n\nEach is the full official npm package: classic WebGL and WebGPU builds, TSL,\nall addons, source modules, fonts, Draco and Basis decoders, and the license.\nThe versioned packages are upstream distributions, without the shared stack's\nlocal patches or WebGL-only exclusions.\n\nThe shelf also pins **Three.js 0.160.0** and older **Rapier 3D compat** releases:\n**0.14.0** for The Ash-Bound Prophecy and **0.19.0** for Ashbound: The Sleeper’s\nOath. These are full official packages, preserved on every sync so the games\nretain their original WebGL renderer and physics.\nThe r160 browser fixture exercises classic WebGL and addons; newer releases\nalso exercise the modern WebGPU build and TSL.\n\nRapier includes **0.19.3, 0.20.0 and 0.21.0** for all 12 official packages:\n\n| Dimension | Standard | SIMD | Deterministic |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2D | `rapier2d`, `rapier2d-compat` | `rapier2d-simd`, `rapier2d-simd-compat` | `rapier2d-deterministic`, `rapier2d-deterministic-compat` |\n| 3D | `rapier3d`, `rapier3d-compat` | `rapier3d-simd`, `rapier3d-simd-compat` | `rapier3d-deterministic`, `rapier3d-deterministic-compat` |\n\nAll package names have the `@dimforge/` scope. Stable releases are included;\nnightly/canary builds are outside this shelf. The starting version `0.193`\nwas interpreted as the published release `0.19.3`.\n\n## Importing games\n\nUse `pnpm ingest <file|folder|zip>`. The importer rewrites recognized Three.js\nand Rapier URLs in HTML, JavaScript and CSS to local paths. Supported hosts:\njsDelivr (npm and Three.js GitHub tags), unpkg, esm.sh, Skypack, JSPM, cdnjs,\nand the official Three.js build/examples paths.\n\nExact version pins stay exact. Partial versions and `^0.x`/`~0.x` ranges select\na compatible local patch. Unmapped bare imports use the detected package\nversion, or the latest version in `manifest.json` when none is specified;\nunversioned CDN references also use the latest. The importer adds per-version\nimport-map scopes so addons and TSL resolve their own version of Three.js.\nExisting mappings, game assets, embedded bundles and game logic are retained.\nThe dry-run report lists dependencies that would become local. Re-importing\nthe same input still skips it as a duplicate.\n\nUnavailable releases and files are reported and left unchanged. A URL for an\nold global `three.min.js` build is not silently replaced by an ES module:\nthose global builds are not part of r180 onward. Arbitrary missing game files,\nother libraries, custom CDN-generated bundles, or incompatible game code still\nneed individual attention. Installing engines cannot supply missing models,\ntextures, levels or audio.\n\n## Manual paths\n=====\n37:| `<meta name=\"description\">` | The blurb in the drawer |\n38:| `<meta name=\"theme-color\">` | That cabinet's marquee colour and the light it throws |\n40:| `<meta property=\"og:image\">` | Its cover art, in a project folder that ships the image |\n164:  folder. A zip of several single-file games becomes a collection. A package\n216:**Size.** GitHub refuses any single file over 100 MB and warns above 50 MB;\n358:The hub as a console's home screen, for a TV and a controller. One game at a\n368:| | Keyboard | Controller |\n389:random games, like a console's attract mode.\n489:In short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\n592:After the picks, **Random Mode** deals. The hub deals every game that declares `hub:session` and\n623:  the browser, as `localStorage['ai-hub:relay-only']`).\n624:- While no game in the library declares `hub:session`, the reference games\n734:own, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\n741:an override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n757:checks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n758:(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DJp2VMNszpzgXYrfLjSPGL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
