{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014YJnDMDaRiUtwHHpppNUvE","type":"tool_result","content":"52:  `csm/CSMShadowNode.js`, `lines/webgpu/Line2.js`.\n75:await kit.renderer.compileAsync(scene, camera);   // optional: no shader hitches on the first frames\n102:  a `count` on repeats, `ready`, `bootMs`, `pipelines`, `pipelineLog`) for\n111:| `kit.tier` | `{ name, pixelRatio, msaa, shadowMapSize, post, detail, drawDistance }` |\n112:| `kit.onQuality(fn)` | the player changed quality: re-apply shadow sizes, counts, draw distance |\n113:| `kit.shadow(light, 2048)` | size a light's shadow map for the tier (2048 at *high*) and keep it sized when quality changes; `kit.shadowSize(2048)` gives just the number |\n136:| shadow map (for a game that uses 2048 at high) | 512 | 1024 | 2048 | 4096 |\n144:look stays on at every tier: bloom on a neon game, fog, outlines, toon\n147:needs to drop an expensive extra (screen-space reflections, a second shadow\n253:`MeshPhongMaterial`, `MeshToonMaterial`, `SpriteMaterial`, `LineBasicMaterial`…)\n261:| `material.onBeforeCompile` | the same node slots on the node material |\n262:| `EffectComposer` + passes | `kit/post.js` (`createPost`) or `THREE.RenderPipeline` with TSL: `bloom`, `fxaa`, `smaa`, `ao` (GTAO), `ssao`, `outline`, `dof`, `film`, `rgbShift`, `chromaticAberration`, `afterImage`, \n263:| `THREE.Points` with `size > 1` | `kit/points.js` (`createPoints`) — WebGPU draws `Points` at 1 px. A background starfield stays opaque (`transparent: false`, `depthWrite: false`, `object.renderOrder = -1`) so it dr\n264:| `PCFSoftShadowMap` | `PCFShadowMap` (set `light.shadow.radius` for softness) or `VSMShadowMap` |\n268:| `Sky`, `Water`, `Reflector`, `Lensflare`, `CSM`, `Line2` (WebGL) | `SkyMesh`, `WaterMesh`, `reflector()`, `LensflareMesh`, `CSMShadowNode`, `lines/webgpu/Line2.js` |\n277:         instanceIndex, vertexColor, hash, mx_noise_float, triNoise3D, select } from 'three/tsl';\n295:| per-instance data | `instanceIndex`, `instancedBufferAttribute(attr)` |\n312:  intensities by `Math.PI`, and for point/spot lights also set `decay = 1`\n323:  `PostProcessing` → `RenderPipeline`, `pass.setResolution` → `setResolutionScale`,\n324:  `useLegacyLights` gone.\n325:- The first frames compile pipelines. Call `await kit.renderer.compileAsync(scene, camera)`\n327:  meshes in the scene) so the first explosion does not stutter. Each pipeline\n330:  (`window.__kit.bootMs`, `pipelines`), so keep the count of distinct\n333:  the pipeline. Prefer uniforms and visibility over creating materials mid-game.\n335:  `InstancedMesh` for repeated props, merge static geometry\n342:  the WebGPU backend (different clip-space depth) and with reversed depth, so\n351:- **One InstancedMesh per chunk, tile or creature compiles shaders every\n352:  time.** In r186 each InstancedMesh puts its uuid into the shader cache key\n354:  shader programs (and pipelines). A streaming world that builds one per\n355:  chunk stalls on compiles (Verdant went from 54 to 2 fps). Batches that\n356:  move: create them with `kit.instanced(geometry, material, capacity)`, which\n359:  went from 472 pipelines to 34). Batches that never move after they are\n360:  built: `bakeInstances(mesh)` from `kit/instancing.js` merges one into a\n361:  plain mesh (instance colours become vertex colours). `__kit.pipelines` counts pipelines: a healthy game stays in the\n362:  tens, and `__kit.pipelineLog` names the material and object of the last 30.\n374:- **A shadow rendered on demand (`shadow.autoUpdate = false`) must keep its\n375:  size.** Resizing its map after the first render (which `kit.shadow()`\n377:  depth texture on WebGPU, every frame (\"Destroyed texture\n378:  ShadowDepthTexture used in a submit\"); a `needsUpdate` or a few frames of\n379:  auto-update don't cure it. Size such shadows once at load","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9652e092-8cd1-4acd-9328-de6431071aa9","uuid":"ff0eb84b-2ad1-482