{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjE3eb2TBrB3Z52g4Uix","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E7EsafUFcGVW9CPybHZteK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211950__xd6e5e2/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np=open('PLAN.md').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global p\n    assert a in p, a[:70]\n    p=p.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# 3.1 fonts + hub kit note\nrep(\"| Fonts | `@fontsource/uncial-antiqua` (titles, 20 KB) and `@fontsource/alegreya` 500/800 (all UI text, 24 KB each), OFL, inlined as base64 woff2. Credit them in About/Credits |\",\n    \"| Fonts | `@fontsource/uncial-antiqua` (titles, 20 KB) and `@fontsource/alegreya` 500/800 (all UI text, 24 KB each), OFL, inlined as base64 woff2 from each package's `files/*-latin-*-normal.woff2`. Credit them in About/Credits. These subsets have no symbols like ▲▼◆★, so draw symbols as inline SVG |\")\nrep(\"| Packaging | One HTML file, no external requests. TASK.md allows CDNs, but inline is simpler and verified on `file://` (3.2 MB for the renderer, Rapier and a test scene) |\",\n    \"| Packaging | One HTML file, no external requests. TASK.md allows CDNs, but inline is simpler and verified on `file://` (3.2 MB for the renderer, Rapier and a test scene) |\\n\\nThe hub repo also has a `lib/kit` built on a newer three.js. Do not use it: TASK.md pins R180.\")\n# 3.2\nrep(\"| Add `--use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader` | **Use this.** WebGPU stays alive, `page.screenshot()` and `canvas.toDataURL()` show real pixels (`--use-angle=swiftshader` is the part that matters) |\",\n    \"| Add `--use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader` | **Use this.** WebGPU stays alive, and `page.screenshot()` and `canvas.toDataURL()` show real pixels, so TASK.md's warning about blank screenshots no longer applies (`--use-angle=swiftshader` is the part that matters) |\")\nrep(\"about 3–5 fps on WebGPU, 2 fps on Chromium WebGL2, 4 fps on WebKit.\",\"about 2–5 fps on WebGPU, 2 fps on Chromium WebGL2, 4 fps on WebKit.\")\n# 3.3 table wording\nrep(\"| `light.visible = false`, add or remove a light | 2 per lit material | Never at runtime |\",\"| `light.visible = false`, or adding a light | Rebuilds every lit pipeline | Never at runtime |\")\nrep(\"| Toggle a light's `castShadow` | 2–3 per lit material | Decide at load and never change |\",\"| Toggle a light's `castShadow` | Rebuilds every lit pipeline | Decide at load and never change |\")\nrep(\"Other r180 facts: `MeshToonNodeMaterial` with a `DataTexture` gradient works. `material.emissiveNode` and `material.maskNode` work on both backends (recipes in Appendix A). `interleavedGradientNoise` is **not** exported from `three/tsl` in r180. `PostProcessing` is the class name in r180 (later releases rename it, so ignore newer docs). WebGPU draws `Points` at 1 px, so use instanced quads for particles. `LineLoop` is not supported. Call `await renderer.compileAsync(scene, camera)` behind the zone-load veil so the first explosion does not stall, and keep one instance of every FX material in the scene when you do.\",\n\"\"\"Two traps that give **no error**, only a wrong picture (both verified on both backends):\n- **`renderer.compileAsync(scene, camera)` before the post chain makes the scene pass draw nothing but the background.** Do not call it. To avoid first-use stalls, build the zone behind the loading veil with one instance of every FX material in view, and render one real frame with `post.render()`.\n- **Inside a post-processing `Fn`, `cameraNear`, `cameraFar`, `cameraProjectionMatrixInverse` and `cameraWorldMatrix` are the full-screen quad's camera, not your scene camera.** Bind uniforms to the scene camera instead, as in A.4. Checked numerically: the reconstructed world position then matches a CPU ray cast to within 0.03 u and stays correct when the camera pans.\n\nOther r180 facts: `MeshToonNodeMaterial` with a `DataTexture` gradient works. `material.emissiveNode` and `material.maskNode` work on both backends (recipes in Appendix A). `interleavedGradientNoise` is **not** exported from `three/tsl` in r180. `PostProcessing` is the class name in r180 (later releases rename it, so ignore newer docs). The hub's notes for a newer three.js say WebGPU draws `Points` at 1 px and does not support `LineLoop`. The planner did not re-test those on r180, so use instanced quads for particles and avoid `LineLoop`.\"\"\")\n# 3.6\nrep(\"Codes are about 860 characters without STUN.\",\"Codes are about 860 characters without STUN. With a public STUN server, the offer grew to about 1,050 characters, gathering ran into the 3 s cap, and the pages still connected.\")\n# 4.2 clock\nrep(\"- **Sim clock:** a `setTimeout` scheduler, not `requestAnimationFrame`, stepping from elapsed time with catch-up capped at 15 ticks per call.\",\"- **Sim clock:** a timer (`setInterval`), not `requestAnimationFrame`, stepping from elapsed time with catch-up capped at 15 ticks per call.\")\n# 5.4 camera\nrep(\"default distance about 24 u, hero about 9% of screen height at 1080p.\",\"default distance about 30 u (a 2 u hero is then about 9% of screen height, verified), which shows about 28 u across the ground.\")\n# passive rename\nrep(\"Overburn Discipline (+20 limit, the first 20 free)\",\"Practised Overburn (+20 limit)\")\n# 7 loadouts\nrep(\"Any skill may sit in any slot. Changing skills costs nothing out of combat.\",\"Any skill may sit in any slot. Changing skills costs nothing out of combat. In each class, the Session loadout below is also what the attract mode and the hub round start with, with one Glyph on each skill.\")\n# 10.1 sizes\nrep(\"**Generator (`src/sim/levelgen.js`).** Seeded. Interiors: graph of ASCII room stamps connected through door sockets on a coarse grid, critical path to the exit, side rooms for loot, events and shrines. Exteriors: a grid of chunk stamps with matching road edges.\",\n    \"**Generator (`src/sim/levelgen.js`).** Seeded. Tile 4 u. Interiors: graph of ASCII room stamps (5–12 tiles across) connected through door sockets on a coarse grid, critical path to the exit, side rooms for loot, events and shrines. Exteriors: a grid of 40×40 u chunk stamps with matching road edges.\")\n# 10.5 feats\nrep(\"Campaign, The Hours, Couch and Online Party on its own (§18.8–9), Hub round \\\"The Last Toll\\\" (§18), Attract (§16), Dev (§17).\",\n    \"Campaign, The Hours, Couch and Online Party on its own (§18.8–9), Hub round \\\"The Last Toll\\\" (§18), Attract (§16), Dev (§17).\\n\\n**Feats:** write about 12 (beat the Chandler without touching burning wax, kill a Tithe Imp, fill a 50-voice CARNAGE, raise a full choir). A toast when earned, listed in the Journal.\")\n# 12.7 cinematics\nrep(\"---\\n\\n## 13. Animation\",\"\"\"### 12.7 Cinematics\n\nReal-time dioramas, not video: a few silhouetted figures and kit props against a flat lit backdrop, with a slow camera push, all through the ink filter so they read as moving woodcuts. Voiced with subtitles, skippable by holding ✕, Enter or a click. Needed: the opening (§11), three act cards with short scenes, the end scene over dawn, then rolling credits.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Animation\"\"\")\n# 15 screens\nrep(\"| Settings | Tabs: Video (render scale, ink strength, shake, flash reduction),\",\"| Settings | Tabs: Video (fullscreen, render scale, ink strength, shake, flash reduction),\")\nrep(\"| Margin Page | Corner page plate, narrated, play continues |\",\"| Margin Page | Corner page plate, narrated, play continues |\\n| Zone veil | Ink wash, a line from the Margin Pages, a guttering candle, while the next zone builds |\")\n# 18.1 head\nrep(\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n\"\"\",\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n\"\"\")\n# 19.1\nrep(\"Keep one or two browsers open at a time and close them. Keep every file inside your own folder, not `/tmp`. Do not run `playwright install`.\",\n    \"Browser tests can use the system Python's Playwright, or `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder. Keep one or two browsers open at a time and close them. Keep every file inside your own folder, not `/tmp`, and do not read files outside it that you do not need, because other agents work in the folders beside yours. Do not run `playwright install`.\")\n# 19.4 hash\nrep(\"for 1.4.0, or the current release if the hub updated)\",\"for 1.4.0; if the hub has released a newer client, the hash is in `RELEASES` in the hub repo's `scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs`)\")\nrep(\"no never-use names (§2) anywhere in `src/` other than the allowed fields.\",\"none of the proper names from §2 anywhere in `src/` other than the allowed fields.\")\n# A.4 recipe\nrep(\"\"\"import { pass, mrt, output, normalView, uv, vec2, vec3, vec4, Fn, abs, max, mix, smoothstep, step,\n         luminance, length, fract, clamp, time, uniform, getViewPosition, perspectiveDepthToViewZ,\n         cameraNear, cameraFar, cameraProjectionMatrixInverse, cameraWorldMatrix, screenSize,\n         mx_noise_float, floor } from 'three/tsl';\"\"\",\"\"\"import { pass, mrt, output, normalView, uv, vec2, vec3, vec4, Fn, abs, max, mix, smoothstep, step,\n         luminance, length, fract, clamp, time, uniform, getViewPosition, perspectiveDepthToViewZ,\n         screenSize, mx_noise_float, floor } from 'three/tsl';\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"const inkStrength = uniform(1);\nconst post\"\"\",\"\"\"const inkStrength = uniform(1);\n// The scene camera, on purpose: cameraNear, cameraWorldMatrix etc. would be the full-screen quad's camera here.\nconst near = uniform(camera.near), far = uniform(camera.far);\nconst projInv = uniform(camera.projectionMatrixInverse), camWorld = uniform(camera.matrixWorld);\nconst post\"\"\")\nrep(\"const viewZ = (p) => perspectiveDepthToViewZ(rawDepth(p), cameraNear, cameraFar);\",\"const viewZ = (p) => perspectiveDepthToViewZ(rawDepth(p), near, far);\")\nrep(\"\"\"  const vp = getViewPosition(p, rawDepth(p), cameraProjectionMatrixInverse);\n  const wp = cameraWorldMatrix.mul(vec4(vp, 1)).xyz;\"\"\",\"\"\"  const vp = getViewPosition(p, rawDepth(p), projInv);\n  const wp = camWorld.mul(vec4(vp, 1)).xyz;\n  const notSky = step(rawDepth(p), 0.9999);\"\"\")\nrep(\"const hatch = max(h1.mul(smoothstep(0.16, 0.07, lum)), h2.mul(smoothstep(0.07, 0.025, lum))).mul(0.55).mul(inkStrength);\",\"const hatch = max(h1.mul(smoothstep(0.16, 0.07, lum)), h2.mul(smoothstep(0.07, 0.025, lum))).mul(0.55).mul(inkStrength).mul(notSky);\")\nrep(\"Emissive colours above 1 feed the bloom. Tune thresholds and hatch frequency by eye.\",\"Set `camera.near` and `camera.far` before building the chain, or update the two uniforms if they change. Emissive colours above 1 feed the bloom. Tune thresholds and hatch frequency by eye.\")\nopen('PLAN.md','w').write(p)\nEOF\ncd .spike && python3 extract.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('a3.mjs').read()\ns=s.replace(\"export function materials(THREE_, mat, wall){\",\"export function materials(){\\n  const mkBands=null;\")\ns=s.replace(\"// rim + hit flash, per object through a uniform\",\"const mat = toon(0xaa8844); const wall = toon(0x777777);\\n// rim + hit flash, per object through a uniform\")\ns=s.replace(\"return { toon, flash, heroUV };\",\"return { toon, flash, heroUV, mat, wall };\")\nopen('a3.mjs','w').write(s)\ns=open('appendix.js').read()\ns=s.replace(\"  await renderer.compileAsync(scene, camera);\\n\",\"\")\n# real content so the hatch can be judged: pillars, tiles, dark corners, no point lights near the far side\ns=s.replace(\"  flash.value = 0.5;\",\"\"\"  flash.value = 0.5;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 40; i++) { const c = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(.5, .6, 5, 10), toon(0x6c6458)); c.position.set(((i * 37) % 40) - 20, 2.5, ((i * 53) % 40) - 20); c.castShadow = true; c.receiveShadow = true; scene.add(c); }\"\"\")\nopen('appendix.js','w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode build.mjs appendix.js appendix.html 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-120; python3 -u run3.py 2>&1 | tail -4 | cut -c1-420","description":"Apply review fixes to plan, re-extract and rerun corrected recipes","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3124,"cache_read_input_tokens":371939,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3124},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9652e092-8cd1-4acd-9328-de6431071aa9","uuid":"fa6457db-59cc-462c-92a9-beba2108932d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:26:44.890Z","request_id":"req_011CgjE3e1YPDd971vTeHtsJ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01E7EsafUFcGVW9CPybHZteK":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211950__xd6e5e2/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np=open('PLAN.md').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global p\n    assert a in p, a[:70]\n    p=p.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# 3.1 fonts + hub kit note\nrep(\"| Fonts | `@fontsource/uncial-antiqua` (titles, 20 KB) and `@fontsource/alegreya` 500/800 (all UI text, 24 KB each), OFL, inlined as base64 woff2. Credit them in About/Credits |\",\n    \"| Fonts | `@fontsource/uncial-antiqua` (titles, 20 KB) and `@fontsource/alegreya` 500/800 (all UI text, 24 KB each), OFL, inlined as base64 woff2 from each package's `files/*-latin-*-normal.woff2`. Credit them in About/Credits. These subsets have no symbols like ▲▼◆★, so draw symbols as inline SVG |\")\nrep(\"| Packaging | One HTML file, no external requests. TASK.md allows CDNs, but inline is simpler and verified on `file://` (3.2 MB for the renderer, Rapier and a test scene) |\",\n    \"| Packaging | One HTML file, no external requests. TASK.md allows CDNs, but inline is simpler and verified on `file://` (3.2 MB for the renderer, Rapier and a test scene) |\\n\\nThe hub repo also has a `lib/kit` built on a newer three.js. Do not use it: TASK.md pins R180.\")\n# 3.2\nrep(\"| Add `--use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader` | **Use this.** WebGPU stays alive, `page.screenshot()` and `canvas.toDataURL()` show real pixels (`--use-angle=swiftshader` is the part that matters) |\",\n    \"| Add `--use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader` | **Use this.** WebGPU stays alive, and `page.screenshot()` and `canvas.toDataURL()` show real pixels, so TASK.md's warning about blank screenshots no longer applies (`--use-angle=swiftshader` is the part that matters) |\")\nrep(\"about 3–5 fps on WebGPU, 2 fps on Chromium WebGL2, 4 fps on WebKit.\",\"about 2–5 fps on WebGPU, 2 fps on Chromium WebGL2, 4 fps on WebKit.\")\n# 3.3 table wording\nrep(\"| `light.visible = false`, add or remove a light | 2 per lit material | Never at runtime |\",\"| `light.visible = false`, or adding a light | Rebuilds every lit pipeline | Never at runtime |\")\nrep(\"| Toggle a light's `castShadow` | 2–3 per lit material | Decide at load and never change |\",\"| Toggle a light's `castShadow` | Rebuilds every lit pipeline | Decide at load and never change |\")\nrep(\"Other r180 facts: `MeshToonNodeMaterial` with a `DataTexture` gradient works. `material.emissiveNode` and `material.maskNode` work on both backends (recipes in Appendix A). `interleavedGradientNoise` is **not** exported from `three/tsl` in r180. `PostProcessing` is the class name in r180 (later releases rename it, so ignore newer docs). WebGPU draws `Points` at 1 px, so use instanced quads for particles. `LineLoop` is not supported. Call `await renderer.compileAsync(scene, camera)` behind the zone-load veil so the first explosion does not stall, and keep one instance of every FX material in the scene when you do.\",\n\"\"\"Two traps that give **no error**, only a wrong picture (both verified on both backends):\n- **`renderer.compileAsync(scene, camera)` before the post chain makes the scene pass draw nothing but the background.** Do not call it. To avoid first-use stalls, build the zone behind the loading veil with one instance of every FX material in view, and render one real frame with `post.render()`.\n- **Inside a post-processing `Fn`, `cameraNear`, `cameraFar`, `cameraProjectionMatrixInverse` and `cameraWorldMatrix` are the full-screen quad's camera, not your scene camera.** Bind uniforms to the scene camera instead, as in A.4. Checked numerically: the reconstructed world position then matches a CPU ray cast to within 0.03 u and stays correct when the camera pans.\n\nOther r180 facts: `MeshToonNodeMaterial` with a `DataTexture` gradient works. `material.emissiveNode` and `material.maskNode` work on both backends (recipes in Appendix A). `interleavedGradientNoise` is **not** exported from `three/tsl` in r180. `PostProcessing` is the class name in r180 (later releases rename it, so ignore newer docs). The hub's notes for a newer three.js say WebGPU draws `Points` at 1 px and does not support `LineLoop`. The planner did not re-test those on r180, so use instanced quads for particles and avoid `LineLoop`.\"\"\")\n# 3.6\nrep(\"Codes are about 860 characters without STUN.\",\"Codes are about 860 characters without STUN. With a public STUN server, the offer grew to about 1,050 characters, gathering ran into the 3 s cap, and the pages still connected.\")\n# 4.2 clock\nrep(\"- **Sim clock:** a `setTimeout` scheduler, not `requestAnimationFrame`, stepping from elapsed time with catch-up capped at 15 ticks per call.\",\"- **Sim clock:** a timer (`setInterval`), not `requestAnimationFrame`, stepping from elapsed time with catch-up capped at 15 ticks per call.\")\n# 5.4 camera\nrep(\"default distance about 24 u, hero about 9% of screen height at 1080p.\",\"default distance about 30 u (a 2 u hero is then about 9% of screen height, verified), which shows about 28 u across the ground.\")\n# passive rename\nrep(\"Overburn Discipline (+20 limit, the first 20 free)\",\"Practised Overburn (+20 limit)\")\n# 7 loadouts\nrep(\"Any skill may sit in any slot. Changing skills costs nothing out of combat.\",\"Any skill may sit in any slot. Changing skills costs nothing out of combat. In each class, the Session loadout below is also what the attract mode and the hub round start with, with one Glyph on each skill.\")\n# 10.1 sizes\nrep(\"**Generator (`src/sim/levelgen.js`).** Seeded. Interiors: graph of ASCII room stamps connected through door sockets on a coarse grid, critical path to the exit, side rooms for loot, events and shrines. Exteriors: a grid of chunk stamps with matching road edges.\",\n    \"**Generator (`src/sim/levelgen.js`).** Seeded. Tile 4 u. Interiors: graph of ASCII room stamps (5–12 tiles across) connected through door sockets on a coarse grid, critical path to the exit, side rooms for loot, events and shrines. Exteriors: a grid of 40×40 u chunk stamps with matching road edges.\")\n# 10.5 feats\nrep(\"Campaign, The Hours, Couch and Online Party on its own (§18.8–9), Hub round \\\"The Last Toll\\\" (§18), Attract (§16), Dev (§17).\",\n    \"Campaign, The Hours, Couch and Online Party on its own (§18.8–9), Hub round \\\"The Last Toll\\\" (§18), Attract (§16), Dev (§17).\\n\\n**Feats:** write about 12 (beat the Chandler without touching burning wax, kill a Tithe Imp, fill a 50-voice CARNAGE, raise a full choir). A toast when earned, listed in the Journal.\")\n# 12.7 cinematics\nrep(\"---\\n\\n## 13. Animation\",\"\"\"### 12.7 Cinematics\n\nReal-time dioramas, not video: a few silhouetted figures and kit props against a flat lit backdrop, with a slow camera push, all through the ink filter so they read as moving woodcuts. Voiced with subtitles, skippable by holding ✕, Enter or a click. Needed: the opening (§11), three act cards with short scenes, the end scene over dawn, then rolling credits.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Animation\"\"\")\n# 15 screens\nrep(\"| Settings | Tabs: Video (render scale, ink strength, shake, flash reduction),\",\"| Settings | Tabs: Video (fullscreen, render scale, ink strength, shake, flash reduction),\")\nrep(\"| Margin Page | Corner page plate, narrated, play continues |\",\"| Margin Page | Corner page plate, narrated, play continues |\\n| Zone veil | Ink wash, a line from the Margin Pages, a guttering candle, while the next zone builds |\")\n# 18.1 head\nrep(\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n\"\"\",\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n\"\"\")\n# 19.1\nrep(\"Keep one or two browsers open at a time and close them. Keep every file inside your own folder, not `/tmp`. Do not run `playwright install`.\",\n    \"Browser tests can use the system Python's Playwright, or `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder. Keep one or two browsers open at a time and close them. Keep every file inside your own folder, not `/tmp`, and do not read files outside it that you do not need, because other agents work in the folders beside yours. Do not run `playwright install`.\")\n# 19.4 hash\nrep(\"for 1.4.0, or the current release if the hub updated)\",\"for 1.4.0; if the hub has released a newer client, the hash is in `RELEASES` in the hub repo's `scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs`)\")\nrep(\"no never-use names (§2) anywhere in `src/` other than the allowed fields.\",\"none of the proper names from §2 anywhere in `src/` other than the allowed fields.\")\n# A.4 recipe\nrep(\"\"\"import { pass, mrt, output, normalView, uv, vec2, vec3, vec4, Fn, abs, max, mix, smoothstep, step,\n         luminance, length, fract, clamp, time, uniform, getViewPosition, perspectiveDepthToViewZ,\n         cameraNear, cameraFar, cameraProjectionMatrixInverse, cameraWorldMatrix, screenSize,\n         mx_noise_float, floor } from 'three/tsl';\"\"\",\"\"\"import { pass, mrt, output, normalView, uv, vec2, vec3, vec4, Fn, abs, max, mix, smoothstep, step,\n         luminance, length, fract, clamp, time, uniform, getViewPosition, perspectiveDepthToViewZ,\n         screenSize, mx_noise_float, floor } from 'three/tsl';\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"const inkStrength = uniform(1);\nconst post\"\"\",\"\"\"const inkStrength = uniform(1);\n// The scene camera, on purpose: cameraNear, cameraWorldMatrix etc. would be the full-screen quad's camera here.\nconst near = uniform(camera.near), far = uniform(camera.far);\nconst projInv = uniform(camera.projectionMatrixInverse), camWorld = uniform(camera.matrixWorld);\nconst post\"\"\")\nrep(\"const viewZ = (p) => perspectiveDepthToViewZ(rawDepth(p), cameraNear, cameraFar);\",\"const viewZ = (p) => perspectiveDepthToViewZ(rawDepth(p), near, far);\")\nrep(\"\"\"  const vp = getViewPosition(p, rawDepth(p), cameraProjectionMatrixInverse);\n  const wp = cameraWorldMatrix.mul(vec4(vp, 1)).xyz;\"\"\",\"\"\"  const vp = getViewPosition(p, rawDepth(p), projInv);\n  const wp = camWorld.mul(vec4(vp, 1)).xyz;\n  const notSky = step(rawDepth(p), 0.9999);\"\"\")\nrep(\"const hatch = max(h1.mul(smoothstep(0.16, 0.07, lum)), h2.mul(smoothstep(0.07, 0.025, lum))).mul(0.55).mul(inkStrength);\",\"const hatch = max(h1.mul(smoothstep(0.16, 0.07, lum)), h2.mul(smoothstep(0.07, 0.025, lum))).mul(0.55).mul(inkStrength).mul(notSky);\")\nrep(\"Emissive colours above 1 feed the bloom. Tune thresholds and hatch frequency by eye.\",\"Set `camera.near` and `camera.far` before building the chain, or update the two uniforms if they change. Emissive colours above 1 feed the bloom. Tune thresholds and hatch frequency by eye.\")\nopen('PLAN.md','w').write(p)\nEOF\ncd .spike && python3 extract.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('a3.mjs').read()\ns=s.replace(\"export function materials(THREE_, mat, wall){\",\"export function materials(){\\n  const mkBands=null;\")\ns=s.replace(\"// rim + hit flash, per object through a uniform\",\"const mat = toon(0xaa8844); const wall = toon(0x777777);\\n// rim + hit flash, per object through a uniform\")\ns=s.replace(\"return { toon, flash, heroUV };\",\"return { toon, flash, heroUV, mat, wall };\")\nopen('a3.mjs','w').write(s)\ns=open('appendix.js').read()\ns=s.replace(\"  await renderer.compileAsync(scene, camera);\\n\",\"\")\n# real content so the hatch can be judged: pillars, tiles, dark corners, no point lights near the far side\ns=s.replace(\"  flash.value = 0.5;\",\"\"\"  flash.value = 0.5;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 40; i++) { const c = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(.5, .6, 5, 10), toon(0x6c6458)); c.position.set(((i * 37) % 40) - 20, 2.5, ((i * 53) % 40) - 20); c.castShadow = true; c.receiveShadow = true; scene.add(c); }\"\"\")\nopen('appendix.js','w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode build.mjs appendix.js appendix.html 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-120; python3 -u run3.py 2>&1 | tail -4 | cut -c1-420","description":"Apply review fixes to plan, re-extract and rerun corrected recipes","timeout":200000}}}
