{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017zqDeSAcTc7G7YxY1WLQPG","type":"tool_result","content":"12:## 1. The game in one page\n35:## 2. What we take from the source, and what we never take\n61:## 3. Verified technical facts\n65:### 3.1 Stack (pinned, verified)\n80:### 3.2 WebGPU in this environment\n93:### 3.3 What rebuilds GPU pipelines in r180 (verified by counting pipeline cr\n113:### 3.4 Physics\n117:### 3.5 AI Hub (verified against the real harness with a prototype: all pass\n128:### 3.6 Serverless online (verified on `file://`)\n132:### 3.7 Touch-only detection (verified on iPhone, iPad and Pixel profiles ag\n138:## 4. Architecture\n140:### 4.1 Layout\n167:### 4.2 The spine: intents in, events out\n183:### 4.3 Data-driven everything (\"normal designer tools\" later)\n187:### 4.4 Saves\n193:## 5. Controls and camera\n197:### 5.1 Controller\n217:### 5.2 Keyboard and mouse (the keys genre players expect)\n240:### 5.3 Prompts\n244:### 5.4 Camera\n252:## 6. Combat model\n281:## 7. Classes\n287:### 7.1 Skill primitives (`src/sim/skills.js`)\n293:### 7.2 The Penitent: bruiser in a rusted confession cage, swinging a bell-c\n311:### 7.3 The Anchorite: walled-up mystic with a crown of candles, robes of me\n329:### 7.4 The Gravecaller: hunched sexton who taught the dead to sing, spade-s\n347:### 7.5 The Nightwarden: lamp-lit hunter of the night roads, wide hat, long \n367:## 8. Monsters\n369:### 8.1 Roster\n398:### 8.2 Elites\n417:### 8.3 Bosses\n454:## 9. Loot and crafting\n495:### 9.1 Tallowgate services (each one simple screen)\n511:## 10. World, zones and modes\n513:### 10.1 Zones\n537:### 10.2 Campaign quests\n557:### 10.3 Difficulty\n568:### 10.4 The Hours (endgame)\n573:### 10.5 Modes at a glance\n581:## 11. Story bible\n642:## 12. Art direction: \"Inked Reliquary\"\n648:### 12.1 Ink filter (recipe in Appendix A, verified on both backends)\n659:### 12.2 Palettes (per zone grade)\n671:### 12.3 Characters\n685:### 12.4 Kits (code-built props; merge static ones by material)\n695:### 12.5 Physics spectacle (`fxWorld`, Rapier)\n699:### 12.6 VFX\n703:### 12.7 Cinematics\n709:## 13. Animation\n732:## 14. Audio\n736:### 14.1 SFX (`src/audio/sfx.js`, patches in data)\n740:### 14.2 Music (`src/audio/music.js`, cues in data)\n755:### 14.3 Voices\n759:### 14.4 Sound checks (no one can listen here)\n765:## 15. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n819:## 16. Attract mode\n842:## 17. Dev mode\n856:## 18. Multiplayer\n858:### 18.1 Hub rules and boot order\n892:### 18.2 The card (the game's own)\n896:### 18.3 The round: \"The Last Toll\"\n918:### 18.4 Wire protocol (`src/net/protocol.js`)\n934:### 18.5 RNG\n938:### 18.6 Render governor\n942:### 18.7 If graphics fail\n946:### 18.8 On its own: couch co-op (up to 4 on one screen)\n950:### 18.9 On its own: online party with invite codes (never in a session)\n959:## 19. Testing\n961:### 19.1 One command\n965:### 19.2 Test API\n969:### 19.3 The bot\n973:### 19.4 What to test\n995:### 19.5 Screenshots\n1001:## 20. Build order\n1035:## 21. Finishing\n1058:## 22. Brief coverage\n1088:## Appendix A: verified recipes\n1092:### A.1 Build (`tools/build.mjs`, shape)\n1103:### A.2 Launch flags\n1111:### A.3 Materials\n1136:### A.4 Ink chain\n1189:### A.5 A rig and a clip\n1204:### A.6 Rapier\n1220:### A.7 Hub boot and host skeleton\n1240:### A.8 Harness driver\n1255:### A.9 Invite codes","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9652e092-8cd1-4acd-9328-de6431071aa9","uuid":"d555ca6c-6e80-4a9f-8623-601691310e83","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:28:00.723Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"12:## 1. The game in one page\n35:## 2. What we take from the source, and what we never take\n61:## 3. Verified technical facts\n65:### 3.1 Stack (pinned, verified)\n80:### 3.2 WebGPU in this environment\n93:### 3.3 What rebuilds GPU pipelines in r180 (verified by counting pipeline cr\n113:### 3.4 Physics\n117:### 3.5 AI Hub (verified against the real harness with a prototype: all pass\n128:### 3.6 Serverless online (verified on `file://`)\n132:### 3.7 Touch-only detection (verified on iPhone, iPad and Pixel profiles ag\n138:## 4. Architecture\n140:### 4.1 Layout\n167:### 4.2 The spine: intents in, events out\n183:### 4.3 Data-driven everything (\"normal designer tools\" later)\n187:### 4.4 Saves\n193:## 5. Controls and camera\n197:### 5.1 Controller\n217:### 5.2 Keyboard and mouse (the keys genre players expect)\n240:### 5.3 Prompts\n244:### 5.4 Camera\n252:## 6. Combat model\n281:## 7. Classes\n287:### 7.1 Skill primitives (`src/sim/skills.js`)\n293:### 7.2 The Penitent: bruiser in a rusted confession cage, swinging a bell-c\n311:### 7.3 The Anchorite: walled-up mystic with a crown of candles, robes of me\n329:### 7.4 The Gravecaller: hunched sexton who taught the dead to sing, spade-s\n347:### 7.5 The Nightwarden: lamp-lit hunter of the night roads, wide hat, long \n367:## 8. Monsters\n369:### 8.1 Roster\n398:### 8.2 Elites\n417:### 8.3 Bosses\n454:## 9. Loot and crafting\n495:### 9.1 Tallowgate services (each one simple screen)\n511:## 10. World, zones and modes\n513:### 10.1 Zones\n537:### 10.2 Campaign quests\n557:### 10.3 Difficulty\n568:### 10.4 The Hours (endgame)\n573:### 10.5 Modes at a glance\n581:## 11. Story bible\n642:## 12. Art direction: \"Inked Reliquary\"\n648:### 12.1 Ink filter (recipe in Appendix A, verified on both backends)\n659:### 12.2 Palettes (per zone grade)\n671:### 12.3 Characters\n685:### 12.4 Kits (code-built props; merge static ones by material)\n695:### 12.5 Physics spectacle (`fxWorld`, Rapier)\n699:### 12.6 VFX\n703:### 12.7 Cinematics\n709:## 13. Animation\n732:## 14. Audio\n736:### 14.1 SFX (`src/audio/sfx.js`, patches in data)\n740:### 14.2 Music (`src/audio/music.js`, cues in data)\n755:### 14.3 Voices\n759:### 14.4 Sound checks (no one can listen here)\n765:## 15. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n819:## 16. Attract mode\n842:## 17. Dev mode\n856:## 18. Multiplayer\n858:### 18.1 Hub rules and bo