{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEAwCqzvVW6ktfj9P6V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VboCB732RHhSUHB1ceK36P","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211950__xd6e5e2/work/PLAN.md","offset":150,"limit":140},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8669,"cache_read_input_tokens":384361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8669},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9652e092-8cd1-4acd-9328-de6431071aa9","uuid":"42da4131-5739-44e9-8feb-5dfb04a6e01d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:28:02.287Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEAvwxym4GT2YZdNCvz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VboCB732RHhSUHB1ceK36P":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211950__xd6e5e2/work/PLAN.md","offset":150,"limit":140}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VboCB732RHhSUHB1ceK36P","type":"tool_result","content":"150\tsrc/main.js               boot order (§18.1)\n151\tsrc/core/                 rng, clock, events, math, save, settings, tuning\n152\tsrc/data/                 every table in this plan, as plain data\n153\tsrc/sim/                  world, actors, combat, skills, status, ai/, bosses/, loot, levelgen, nav,\n154\t                          quests, events, hours, bot. NO DOM, NO three. Runs in Node.\n155\tsrc/view/                 renderer, ink, materials, camera, lights, kit/, rigs/, anim/, fx/,\n156\t                          decals, fxphysics (ragdolls, debris), actorsView, levelView\n157\tsrc/audio/                engine, reverb, music, sfx, voice\n158\tsrc/input/                devices, actions, pad, kbm, glyphs\n159\tsrc/ui/                   ui stack, focus, hud, prompts, icons, style.css, screens/\n160\tsrc/net/                  net interface, hubNet, peerNet, localNet, replicate, outbox, protocol\n161\tsrc/modes/                campaign, hours, session, attract, dev\n162\ttests/                    data/, sim/, browser/, hub/\n163\tdocs/CONTENT.md           how to add a monster, skill, item, room, quest, line of dialogue\n164\tdist/game.html            build output; copy to the name and place TASK.md requires\n165\t```\n166\t\n167\t### 4.2 The spine: intents in, events out\n168\t\n169\t```\n170\tinput / bot / network  ->  Intent per player per tick  ->  Sim (fixed 30 Hz)  ->  Event stream + plain-data state\n171\t                                                                                     |-> View (draws, sounds, fx, ragdolls)\n172\t                                                                                     |-> Net (replicates to clients)\n173\t                                                                                     |-> Tests (assert on it)\n174\t```\n175\t\n176\t- **Sim** is plain data and logic, seeded RNG streams only (`rng('loot')`, `rng('world')`), never `Math.random`. It runs headless in Node, on the hub's playerless server copy, and at high speed in tests. It reads nothing from the GPU. Cosmetic code in the view may use `Math.random`.\n177\t- **Intent:** `{mx, mz, moveTo, aimX, aimZ, pressed:[...], held:[...]}`. Pad, mouse, keyboard, bot, attract and network all produce the same thing.\n178\t- **Events:** `hit, death, cast, status, drop, pickup, levelup, quest, say, toll, spawn, break, telegraph, ...`. The view and the network consume the same stream. A client copy feeds received events into the same view code.\n179\t- **Two Rapier worlds.** `simWorld` in the sim: static colliders, actor capsules, character controllers, ray and shape queries. `fxWorld` in the view: ragdolls, gibs, furniture debris, coins, falling chandeliers, tipping vats. `fxWorld` is cosmetic and local to each copy, so it never needs syncing and the server copy has none. A chandelier's damage is a scripted timer and radius in the sim, and its fall is Rapier in the view.\n180\t- **Sim clock:** a timer (`setInterval`), not `requestAnimationFrame`, stepping from elapsed time with catch-up capped at 15 ticks per call. The view interpolates at display rate. A hidden host tab must keep the world running.\n181\t- The sim is 2.5D: gameplay happens in x/z. The view lifts actors onto the visual ground height. Simple, robust, and it matches what the source's camera shows.\n182\t\n183\t### 4.3 Data-driven everything (\"normal designer tools\" later)\n184\t\n185\tEvery class, skill, glyph, monster, affix, item base, legendary, set, room stamp, zone, quest, dialogue, lore page, bark, music cue, sound patch and balance value is a plain data entry in `src/data/`, loaded through one validator (`tests/data`). Rooms are ASCII stamps a designer can edit in a text editor. Skills are composed from effect primitives (§7.1), so a new skill means new data, not new code. Dev mode can export current tuning as JSON. `docs/CONTENT.md` explains in a page how to add each kind of content.\n186\t\n187\t### 4.4 Saves\n188\t\n189\t`localStorage`, one versioned JSON document: 4 hero slots, shared stash and gold, settings, unlocks, tuning overrides. Autosave on zone change, quest step and quit. Wrap all storage in try/catch. In a hub session the client swaps in a memory-only storage, so no special case is needed.\n190\t\n191\t---\n192\t\n193\t## 5. Controls and camera\n194\t\n195\tStandard-mapping buttons: 0 Cross, 1 Circle, 2 Square, 3 Triangle, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad, 16 PS, 17 touchpad. Design for any pad reporting `mapping === 'standard'`. Use a non-standard pad on the same indices as best effort, with a one-time notice that its buttons may differ.\n196\t\n197\t### 5.1 Controller\n198\t\n199\t| Input | In the world | In menus |\n200\t|---|---|---|\n201\t| Left stick | Move (direct, analog speed) | Move focus |\n202\t| Right stick | Aim override: skills fire that way, an arc shows at the hero's feet. Released: auto-aim | Scroll, or spin the hero on the Wheel |\n203\t| ✕ Cross | Slot 1, hold to keep attacking. A **tap** while an interact prompt shows: interact | Confirm |\n204\t| □ Square | Slot 2 | Item action (mark, salvage) |\n205\t| △ Triangle | Slot 3 | Details / compare |\n206\t| ○ Circle | Slot 4 | Back |\n207\t| R1 / R2 | Slot 5 / Slot 6 | Next tab / page down |\n208\t| L1 | Potion | Previous tab |\n209\t| L2 | Evade roll (move direction, else facing) | Page up |\n210\t| D-pad ↑ → ← | Wheel / Psalter / Journal | Move focus |\n211\t| D-pad ↓ (hold) | Homeward Candle | Move focus |\n212\t| Create (tap) or touchpad | Map | |\n213\t| Options | Pause | Back to game |\n214\t\n215\tAuto-aim: best target in a ±35° cone inside the skill's range, weighted by distance and elite status, strength in Dev sliders. Rumble through `gamepad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', ...)`, guarded and toggleable. Deadzones: stick 0.18 radial. Ignore Options while Create is held (the hub owns that chord). Open the map on Create **release**, only if Options was not pressed during the hold.\n216\t\n217\t### 5.2 Keyboard and mouse (the keys genre players expect)\n218\t\n219\t| Input | Action |\n220\t|---|---|\n221\t| Left mouse | Hold to move toward cursor. On a monster: Slot 1 at it. On loot, NPC, door, shrine: walk there and use it |\n222\t| Right mouse | Slot 2 at cursor |\n223\t| 1 2 3 4 | Slots 3–6 at cursor |\n224\t| Q | Potion |\n225\t| Space | Evade roll toward cursor |\n226\t| Shift (hold) | Stand still and attack toward cursor |\n227\t| Alt (hold) | Show all loot labels |\n228\t| I or C | Wheel (inventory) |\n229\t| S or K | Psalter (skills) |\n230\t| J | Journal |\n231\t| M or Tab | Map |\n232\t| T | Homeward Candle |\n233\t| Esc | Pause / back |\n234\t| Enter | Confirm, or use the highlighted thing |\n235\t| Arrow keys | Move directly. WASD too when Settings ▸ Controls ▸ WASD Movement is on (off by default, as `S` is Psalter; K always works) |\n236\t| Wheel | Camera zoom in the world, scroll in menus |\n237\t\n238\tIn the world, **hover highlights** anything usable with an ink-gold outline and a nameplate. In menus, **hover moves the focus**, left click confirms, right click is the item quick action (equip, sell) or back on empty space. Only real mouse movement changes focus, never a menu scrolling under a still cursor. Show a gothic gauntlet cursor (CSS data-URI) and hide it while the controller is the last-used device.\n239\t\n240\t### 5.3 Prompts\n241\t\n242\tEvery on-screen prompt goes through `Glyph(action)`, which resolves from the last-used device: **PlayStation shapes** by default on a pad, **A B X Y / LB RB LT RT / Menu View** with Settings ▸ Controls ▸ Controller Glyphs set to Xbox, and **keycaps and mouse-button icons** for keyboard and mouse. Draw them as inline SVG. Prompts swap instantly on device change, and stick noise under 0.5 must not flip the device. The hotbar labels swap the same way: same bar, same position, different glyphs.\n243\t\n244\t### 5.4 Camera\n245\t\n246\tPerspective, FOV 30°, yaw 45° (diamond grid), pitch about 55°, default distance about 30 u (a 2 u hero is then about 9% of screen height, verified), which shows about 28 u across the ground. Three zoom steps. Critically damped follow with a slight lead toward movement. Pulls back in boss arenas, dollies close with letterbox for dialogue. Shake on big hits, with a Settings slider. In couch co-op it frames all local players and zooms out to a limit (§18.8).\n247\t\n248\t**Occlusion.** Walls whose outward face points at the camera (+x and +z sides) are built as knee-high stubs with an inked cap, the classic isometric cut-away. Tall props in front of the hero use a dithered screen-space hole (`maskNode`, verified, Appendix A).\n249\t\n250\t---\n251\t\n252\t## 6. Combat model\n253\t\n254\tTick 30 Hz. Units: 1 u ≈ 1 m. Hero run speed 6 u/s, evade roll 7 u in 0.45 s with i-frames, cooldown 3 s, two charges.\n255\t\n256\t```\n257\tdamage = weaponDPS × (1 + primary/100) × skillPct × (1 + typeBonus + eliteBonus)\n258\t       × (crit ? critMult : 1) × tuning.playerDamage\n259\tmonsterHP(level) = baseHP × tier × (1 + 0.28 × (level−1)) × difficulty.hp × (1 + 0.75 × (partySize−1))\n260\tmonsterDmg(level) = baseDmg × tier × (1 + 0.18 × (level−1)) × difficulty.dmg\n261\tmitigation = armor / (armor + 50 × monsterLevel), resist likewise with 5 ×\n262\txpToNext(L) = 120 × L^1.6\n263\t```\n264\t\n265\t**Targets to tune against with the bot (§19):** a normal monster dies in 2–3 Slot 1 hits at level parity on Pilgrim; champions in 15–25 hits; a boss fight takes the times in §8.3; a level-appropriate hero survives about 8 normal-monster hits. Level 12 at the end of Act I, 20 at the end of Act II, 24 at the end of the campaign, cap 30 in The Hours.\n266\t\n267\t**Damage types:** Physical, Fire, Holy, Shadow. **Status:** Burn and Bleed (damage over time), Slow, Waxed (slow, three stacks becomes Root), Stun, Root, Fear, Blind (ranged enemies stop firing), Marked (+damage taken), Knockback. Elites take quarter duration on hard control, bosses are immune but build a stagger meter.\n268\t\n269\t**Feel, tuned in Dev:** hit-stop 40–80 ms (scaled, never on the hero's movement), white flash via uniform, knockback slide, ink spatter decal, layered sound, rumble, shake on crits and big kills. Generators land within 0.12–0.2 s of the press. Movement cancels recovery.\n270\t\n271\t**Life:** Vial of Last Light (potion) has unlimited uses on a 30 s cooldown. **Heartsparks** (health globes) drop from kills and drift to you. Gold is collected automatically in a radius. **Death:** \"You have fallen.\" Rise at the last checkpoint, or at your corpse (three times per zone). In co-op, allies revive you with a 2 s hold. **Hardcore toggle (\"Final Hour\")** at hero creation: death ends the hero, who is then listed on a Memorial page.\n272\t\n273\t**Kill bonuses** (big text, XP, cheer sound):\n274\t- **CARNAGE ×N:** kills within 1.5 s of each other, from N ≥ 5.\n275\t- **DEVASTATION:** 8+ kills from one hit.\n276\t- **RUINOUS:** 10+ objects broken in 3 s.\n277\t- **SENT UPWARD:** killing blow launches the corpse far (physics).\n278\t\n279\t---\n280\t\n281\t## 7. Classes\n282\t\n283\tEvery class: 8 active skills, 3 Glyphs per skill (unlock 2, 5 and 9 levels after the skill), 6 passives, 6 action slots, passive slots at levels 5, 10, 15. Any skill may sit in any slot. Changing skills costs nothing out of combat. In each class, the Session loadout below is also what the attract mode and the hub round start with, with one Glyph on each skill. Each class has a code-built rig and silhouette (§12.3), its own resource vial and voice.\n284\t\n285\tHero creation: choose class on a 3D line-up, accept a generated gothic name (△ re-rolls), choose difficulty and the Final Hour toggle. No text entry is needed.\n286\t\n287\t### 7.1 Skill primitives (`src/sim/skills.js`)\n288\t\n289\t`melee_arc{range,arc,pct}`, `projectile{speed,count,spread,pierce,homing,chain,radius}`, `nova{radius,pct,delay}`, `ground{radius,duration,tick,pct,status,follow}`, `beam{length,width,pctPerS,channel}`, `leap{range,radius,pct}`, `dash{range,width,pct,iframes}`, `blink{range}`, `pull{range,count}`, `summon{kind,count,max,duration}`, `buff{stats,duration,aura}`, `trap{arm,radius,pct}`, `turret{duration,rate,projectile}`, `corpse{op}`, `wall{length,duration}`. A skill is a list of these plus cost, cooldown, clip, sound and VFX ids. A Glyph is a data patch on that list. Legendary powers and passives are hooks (`onHit`, `onKill`, `onCast`, `onStruck`, `modifySkill`)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9652e092-8cd1-4acd-9328-de6431071aa9","uuid":"8b131070-513c-45bc-87cc-e6cf0ede1eec","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:28:02.297Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211950__xd6e5e2/work/PLAN.md","content":"src/main.js               boot order (§18.1)\nsrc/core/                 rng, clock, events, math, save, settings, tuning\nsrc/data/                 every table in this plan, as plain data\nsrc/sim/                  world, actors, combat, skills, status, ai/, bosses/, loot, levelgen, nav,\n                          quests, events, hours, bot. NO DOM, NO three. Runs in Node.\nsrc/view/                 renderer, ink, materials, camera, lights, kit/, rigs/, anim/, fx/,\n                          decals, fxphysics (ragdolls, debris), actorsView, levelView\nsrc/audio/                engine, reverb, music, sfx, voice\nsrc/input/                devices, actions, pad, kbm, glyphs\nsrc/ui/                   ui stack, focus, hud, prompts, icons, style.css, screens/\nsrc/net/                  net interface, hubNet, peerNet, localNet, replicate, outbox, protocol\nsrc/modes/                campaign, hours, session, attract, dev\ntests/                    data/, sim/, browser/, hub/\ndocs/CONTENT.md           how to add a monster, skill, item, room, quest, line of dialogue\ndist/game.html            build output; copy to the name and place TASK.md requires\n```\n\n### 4.2 The spine: intents in, events out\n\n```\ninput / bot / network  ->  Intent per player per tick  ->  Sim (fixed 30 Hz)  ->  Event stream + plain-data state\n                                                                                     |-> View (draws, sounds, fx, ragdolls)\n                                                                                     |-> Net (replicates to clients)\n                                                                                     |-> Tests (assert on it)\n```\n\n- **Sim** is plain data and logic, seeded RNG streams only (`rng('loot')`, `rng('world')`), never `Math.random`. It runs headless in Node, on the hub's playerless server copy, and at high speed in tests. It reads nothing from the GPU. Cosmetic code in the view may use `Math.random`.\n- **Intent:** `{mx, mz, moveTo, aimX, aimZ, pressed:[...], held:[...]}`. Pad, mouse, keyboard, bot, attract and network all produce the same thing.\n- **Events:** `hit, death, cast, status, drop, pickup, levelup, quest, say, toll, spawn, break, telegraph, ...`. The view and the network consume the same stream. A client copy feeds received events into the same view code.\n- **Two Rapier worlds.** `simWorld` in the sim: static colliders, actor capsules, character controllers, ray and shape queries. `fxWorld` in the view: ragdolls, gibs, furniture debris, coins, falling chandeliers, tipping vats. `fxWorld` is cosmetic and local to each copy, so it never needs syncing and the server copy has none. A chandelier's damage is a scripted timer and radius in the sim, and its fall is Rapier in the view.\n- **Sim clock:** a timer (`setInterval`), not `requestAnimationFrame`, stepping from elapsed time with catch-up capped at 15 ticks per call. The view interpolates at display rate. A hidden host tab must keep the world running.\n- The sim is 2.5D: gameplay happens in x/z. The view lifts actors onto the visual ground height. Simple, robust, and it matches what the source's camera shows.\n\n### 4.3 Data-driven everything (\"normal designer tools\" later)\n\nEvery class, skill, glyph, monster, affix, item base, legendary, set, room stamp, zone, quest, dialogue, lore page, bark, music cue, sound patch and balance value is a plain data entry in `src/data/`, loaded through one validator (`tests/data`). Rooms are ASCII stamps a designer can edit in a text editor. Skills are composed from effect primitives (§7.1), so a new skill means new data, not new code. Dev mode can export current tuning as JSON. `docs/CONTENT.md` explains in a page how to add each kind of content.\n\n### 4.4 Saves\n\n`localStorage`, one versioned JSON document: 4 hero slots, shared stash and gold, settings, unlocks, tuning overrides. Autosave on zone change, quest step and quit. Wrap all storage in try/catch. In a hub session the client swaps in a memory-only storage, so no special case is needed.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Controls and camera\n\nStandard-mapping buttons: 0 Cross, 1 Circle, 2 Square, 3 Triangle, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad, 16 PS, 17 touchpad. Design for any pad reporting `mapping === 'standard'`. Use a non-standard pad on the same indices as best effort, with a one-time notice that its buttons may differ.\n\n### 5.1 Controller\n\n| Input | In the world | In menus |\n|---|---|---|\n| Left stick | Move (direct, analog speed) | Move focus |\n| Right stick | Aim override: skills fire that way, an arc shows at the hero's feet. Released: auto-aim | Scroll, or spin the hero on the Wheel |\n| ✕ Cross | Slot 1, hold to keep attacking. A **tap** while an interact prompt shows: interact | Confirm |\n| □ Square | Slot 2 | Item action (mark, salvage) |\n| △ Triangle | Slot 3 | Details / compare |\n| ○ Circle | Slot 4 | Back |\n| R1 / R2 | Slot 5 / Slot 6 | Next tab / page down |\n| L1 | Potion | Previous tab |\n| L2 | Evade roll (move direction, else facing) | Page up |\n| D-pad ↑ → ← | Wheel / Psalter / Journal | Move focus |\n| D-pad ↓ (hold) | Homeward Candle | Move focus |\n| Create (tap) or touchpad | Map | |\n| Options | Pause | Back to game |\n\nAuto-aim: best target in a ±35° cone inside the skill's range, weighted by distance and elite status, strength in Dev sliders. Rumble through `gamepad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', ...)`, guarded and toggleable. Deadzones: stick 0.18 radial. Ignore Options while Create is held (the hub owns that chord). Open the map on Create **release**, only if Options was not pressed during the hold.\n\n### 5.2 Keyboard and mouse (the keys genre players expect)\n\n| Input | Action |\n|---|---|\n| Left mouse | Hold to move toward cursor. On a monster: Slot 1 at it. On loot, NPC, door, shrine: walk there and use it |\n| Right mouse | Slot 2 at cursor |\n| 1 2 3 4 | Slots 3–6 at cursor |\n| Q | Potion |\n| Space | Evade roll toward cursor |\n| Shift (hold) | Stand still and attack toward cursor |\n| Alt (hold) | Show all loot labels |\n| I or C | Wheel (inventory) |\n| S or K | Psalter (skills) |\n| J | Journal |\n| M or Tab | Map |\n| T | Homeward Candle |\n| Esc | Pause / back |\n| Enter | Confirm, or use the highlighted thing |\n| Arrow keys | Move directly. WASD too when Settings ▸ Controls ▸ WASD Movement is on (off by default, as `S` is Psalter; K always works) |\n| Wheel | Camera zoom in the world, scroll in menus |\n\nIn the world, **hover highlights** anything usable with an ink-gold outline and a nameplate. In menus, **hover moves the focus**, left click confirms, right click is the item quick action (equip, sell) or back on empty space. Only real mouse movement changes focus, never a menu scrolling under a still cursor. Show a gothic gauntlet cursor (CSS data-URI) and hide it while the controller is the last-used device.\n\n### 5.3 Prompts\n\nEvery on-screen prompt goes through `Glyph(action)`, which resolves from the last-used device: **PlayStation shapes** by default on a pad, **A B X Y / LB RB LT RT / Menu View** with Settings ▸ Controls ▸ Controller Glyphs set to Xbox, and **keycaps and mouse-button icons** for keyboard and mouse. Draw them as inline SVG. Prompts swap instantly on device change, and stick noise under 0.5 must not flip the device. The hotbar labels swap the same way: same bar, same position, different glyphs.\n\n### 5.4 Camera\n\nPerspective, FOV 30°, yaw 45° (diamond grid), pitch about 55°, default distance about 30 u (a 2 u hero is then about 9% of screen height, verified), which shows about 28 u across the ground. Three zoom steps. Critically damped follow with a slight lead toward movement. Pulls back in boss arenas, dollies close with letterbox for dialogue. Shake on big hits, with a Settings slider. In couch co-op it frames all local players and zooms out to a limit (§18.8).\n\n**Occlusion.** Walls whose outward face points at the camera (+x and +z sides) are built as knee-high stubs with an inked cap, the classic isometric cut-away. Tall props in front of the hero use a dithered screen-space hole (`maskNode`, verified, Appendix A).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Combat model\n\nTick 30 Hz. Units: 1 u ≈ 1 m. Hero run speed 6 u/s, evade roll 7 u in 0.45 s with i-frames, cooldown 3 s, two charges.\n\n```\ndamage = weaponDPS × (1 + primary/100) × skillPct × (1 + typeBonus + eliteBonus)\n       × (crit ? critMult : 1) × tuning.playerDamage\nmonsterHP(level) = baseHP × tier × (1 + 0.28 × (level−1)) × difficulty.hp × (1 + 0.75 × (partySize−1))\nmonsterDmg(level) = baseDmg × tier × (1 + 0.18 × (level−1)) × difficulty.dmg\nmitigation = armor / (armor + 50 × monsterLevel), resist likewise with 5 ×\nxpToNext(L) = 120 × L^1.6\n```\n\n**Targets to tune against with the bot (§19):** a normal monster dies in 2–3 Slot 1 hits at level parity on Pilgrim; champions in 15–25 hits; a boss fight takes the times in §8.3; a level-appropriate hero survives about 8 normal-monster hits. Level 12 at the end of Act I, 20 at the end of Act II, 24 at the end of the campaign, cap 30 in The Hours.\n\n**Damage types:** Physical, Fire, Holy, Shadow. **Status:** Burn and Bleed (damage over time), Slow, Waxed (slow, three stacks becomes Root), Stun, Root, Fear, Blind (ranged enemies stop firing), Marked (+damage taken), Knockback. Elites take quarter duration on hard control, bosses are immune but build a stagger meter.\n\n**Feel, tuned in Dev:** hit-stop 40–80 ms (scaled, never on the hero's movement), white flash via uniform, knockback slide, ink spatter decal, layered sound, rumble, shake on crits and big kills. Generators land within 0.12–0.2 s of the press. Movement cancels recovery.\n\n**Life:** Vial of Last Light (potion) has unlimited uses on a 30 s cooldown. **Heartsparks** (health globes) drop from kills and drift to you. Gold is collected automatically in a radius. **Death:** \"You have fallen.\" Rise at the last checkpoint, or at your corpse (three times per zone). In co-op, allies revive you with a 2 s hold. **Hardcore toggle (\"Final Hour\")** at hero creation: death ends the hero, who is then listed on a Memorial page.\n\n**Kill bonuses** (big text, XP, cheer sound):\n- **CARNAGE ×N:** kills within 1.5 s of each other, from N ≥ 5.\n- **DEVASTATION:** 8+ kills from one hit.\n- **RUINOUS:** 10+ objects broken in 3 s.\n- **SENT UPWARD:** killing blow launches the corpse far (physics).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Classes\n\nEvery class: 8 active skills, 3 Glyphs per skill (unlock 2, 5 and 9 levels after the skill), 6 passives, 6 action slots, passive slots at levels 5, 10, 15. Any skill may sit in any slot. Changing skills costs nothing out of combat. In each class, the Session loadout below is also what the attract mode and the hub round start with, with one Glyph on each skill. Each class has a code-built rig and silhouette (§12.3), its own resource vial and voice.\n\nHero creation: choose class on a 3D line-up, accept a generated gothic name (△ re-rolls), choose difficulty and the Final Hour toggle. No text entry is needed.\n\n### 7.1 Skill primitives (`src/sim/skills.js`)\n\n`melee_arc{range,arc,pct}`, `projectile{speed,count,spread,pierce,homing,chain,radius}`, `nova{radius,pct,delay}`, `ground{radius,duration,tick,pct,status,follow}`, `beam{length,width,pctPerS,channel}`, `leap{range,radius,pct}`, `dash{range,width,pct,iframes}`, `blink{range}`, `pull{range,count}`, `summon{kind,count,max,duration}`, `buff{stats,duration,aura}`, `trap{arm,radius,pct}`, `turret{duration,rate,projectile}`, `corpse{op}`, `wall{length,duration}`. A skill is a list of these plus cost, cooldown, clip, sound and VFX ids. A Glyph is a data patch on that list. Legendary powers and passives are hooks (`onHit`, `onKill`, `onCast`, `onStruck`, `modifySkill`).","numLines":140,"startLine":150,"totalLines":1270}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VboCB732RHhSUHB1ceK36P","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
