{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEGaXozCFUmsFChUbcA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` is finished and covers everything in `TASK.md`; section 22 maps each requirement to the section that handles it. `planner-exit-interview.json` is also saved and parses as valid JSON. The game itself isn't built yet, so the checks below ran on throwaway prototypes, which I've since deleted. Nothing is committed.\n\n**The game in the plan:** an isometric co-op action-RPG for 1–4 players, inspired by Diablo 3 but with its own world and cast.\n- **Story:** a black bell falls on an abbey, and its seventh toll will take the sun.\n- **Content:**\n  - four classes, 20 monsters and five bosses\n  - full loot and crafting\n  - a three-act campaign plus replayable endgame runs\n  - about 12 pieces of written lore, with key scenes and sample lines for the rest of the script\n- **Look:** a moving woodcut, with ink outlines and hatching fixed to surfaces.\n- **Left to builders:** the title and file names, and all paths are relative to the dev folder.\n\n**What testing the pinned stack changed:**\n- **`TASK.md`'s WebGPU flags are broken here:** the device dies after the first frame, so frame rates look great and screenshots come out blank. Adding `--use-angle=swiftshader` fixes it, and you may want to correct your template.\n- **Two graphics recipes failed with no error:**\n  - `compileAsync` before the post chain draws an empty scene.\n  - Camera values inside a post pass read the wrong camera.\n  - I fixed both in the plan, then re-ran its recipes as written on WebGPU and WebGL2.\n- **AI Hub:**\n  - A prototype using the plan's boot order passes the real harness at 2, 3 and 4 players, host-leave and server, on both graphics backends.\n  - A heavier scene also passes at 4 players on WebGL2.\n  - The harness can report a pass after an early exit, so the plan also requires a minimum number of checks.\n  - `http.server` buffers its port line when piped, so the plan uses `-u`.\n- **Plan rules from these tests:** which changes rebuild GPU pipelines, how to detect touch-only devices, and invite codes that work with no server.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- **Firefox:** it gave no WebGL context on real pages under Playwright, so the plan just asks for a clear message instead of a crash.\n- **Invite codes:** they connected between two pages on this machine, but not across real networks.\n- **`Points` and `LineLoop`:** those limits come from the hub's notes for a newer three.js, and the plan says so.\n\n**One decision to check:** \"multiplayer for the game on its own\" was ambiguous, so I took the stronger reading and planned couch co-op plus invite codes. If you meant less, the cut rules in section 20 already allow dropping invite codes.\n\nEverything is in the `work` folder:\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `planner-exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":858,"cache_read_input_tokens":407150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":858},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9652e092-8cd1-4acd-9328-de6431071aa9","uuid":"9b164b9c-484e-48be-9a9d-2af7771b99d0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:29:06.801Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEGaFgRTiE1xeM9HKPo"}
