{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TUh2QZULwCWyP7wH1Kyww1","type":"tool_result","content":"1035\t## 21. Finishing\n1036\t\n1037\t**About/Credits screen** (paged, big text, reachable from Main Menu and Pause) and **your final chat reply** both contain, with `unknown` for anything you cannot confirm:\n1038\t\n1039\t- **Source Information:** Date, Source, Plan (the file name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (with versions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage (write exactly `added on import`). Take the Date, Environment and Model from your TASK.md, not from memory.\n1040\t- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback:** every question in TASK.md, with honest answers.\n1041\t- **Credits:** three.js, Rapier, Uncial Antiqua and Alegreya with their licenses.\n1042\t\n1043\tKeep all of it in one file (`src/data/about.js`), so the screen and the exit interview cannot drift apart. **Exit interview:** write the JSON exactly in the shape TASK.md gives, at the place TASK.md names, generated by `tools/make-exit.mjs`, and check it parses. Suggested `aiHub` values: type `Game`, genre `RPG`, source `Diablo 3`, series `Diablo`, players `1–4`, controls `Stick or mouse to move, face buttons or 1-4 for skills, L1 or Q for potion`, tags `3d`, `co-op`, `fantasy`, `boss fights`, `top-down`, `story`. `name` is your title. Suggested tagline: `Seven tolls, and the sun forgets the way`. Suggested description: `An inked co-op action-RPG: cut through candle-headed dead and a tax-collecting devil lord to silence a black bell before the seventh toll.` Use the same tagline in the page `<title>`. Answers to the feedback questions come at the very end, and then you rebuild once more so the screen has them.\n1044\t\n1045\t**Package:** run `node tools/build.mjs`, copy `dist/game.html` to the single HTML name and location your TASK.md requires, run the whole test suite against that final copy.\n1046\t\n1047\t**Done means:**\n1048\t- [ ] Every row of §22 is true.\n1049\t- [ ] Full test suite green against the final file. Whole-campaign bot passes in every class.\n1050\t- [ ] Hub harness passes on all scenarios with no warnings.\n1051\t- [ ] `grep` of `src/` finds no TODO, FIXME, stub or placeholder.\n1052\t- [ ] You looked at screenshots of every zone and screen at 1920×1080.\n1053\t- [ ] About/Credits, the exit interview JSON and your chat reply all agree.\n1054\t- [ ] Your temporary files are gone and all your processes are stopped.\n1055\t\n1056\t---\n1057\t\n1058\t## 22. Brief coverage\n1059\t\n1060\t| TASK.md asks for | Where |\n1061\t|---|---|\n1062\t| Source, original game, world, characters, themes, tone | §1, §2, §11 |\n1063\t| Genre and perspective choice | §1 |\n1064\t| Title: riff, 50 ideas, real RNG | Top of plan, §20 M0 |\n1065\t| Research (your choice) | Planner research is reflected here. Report your own in Source Information |\n1066\t| Single HTML, CDN optional | §3.1, §21 |\n1067\t| Three.js R180, WebGPU, cel/ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API | §3, §12, §14, §5 |\n1068\t| Art direction: engine base, new art for source feel | §12 |\n1069\t| Animation: engine system, new animations | §13 |\n1070\t| Audio: code only, gibberish voices, music 10% | §14 |\n1071\t| Online via AI Hub, in the hub and on its own | §18 |\n1072\t| Dev folder, modules, bundle, shared-machine rules | §4.1, §19.1, §21 |\n1073\t| Performance budget unlimited, no FPS or optimization work | §12 |\n1074\t| Testing: headless, whole-game script, one quiet command, no review subagents | §19 |\n1075\t| Effort: yours to spend | Spend it where the pillars in §1 say it shows |\n1076\t| Feature-complete, long enough, polished slice, infrastructure for designers | §1, §4.3, §20 |\n1077\t| Dev mode from Pause, live sliders, reset | §17 |\n1078\t| Attract at 10 s, looping, any input exits, may cheat | §16 |\n1079\t| Narrative tone like the source | §11 |\n1080\t| 10-foot, DualSense first, native keys and mouse, hover focus, last-input prompts, PlayStation and Xbox glyphs | §5, §15 |\n1081\t| No dense web-style screens | §15 |\n1082\t| Touch-only notice, settings button, attract runs | §15, §16, §3.7 |\n1083\t| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §1, §19.4, §20, §21 |\n1084\t| Source Information, feedback in chat and About/Credits | §21 |\n1085\t| Exit interview JSON | §21 |\n1086\t\n1087\t---\n1088\t\n1089\t## Appendix A: verified recipes\n1090\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9652e092-8cd1-4acd-9328-de6431071aa9","uuid":"eb9c8f78-5cf4-4ee5-9eaf-066053ec06d1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:30:39.487Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211950__xd6e5e2/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 21. Finishing\n\n**About/Credits screen** (paged, big text, reachable from Main Menu and Pause) and **your final chat reply** both contain, with `unknown` for anything you cannot confirm:\n\n- **Source Information:** Date, Source, Plan (the file name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (with versions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage (write exactly `added on import`). Take the Date, Environment and Model from your TASK.md, not from memory.\n- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback:** every question in TASK.md, with honest answers.\n- **Credits:** three.js, Rapier, Uncial Antiqua and Alegreya with their licenses.\n\nKeep all of it in one file (`src/data/about.js`), so the screen and the exit interview cannot drift apart. **Exit interview:** write the JSON exactly in the shape TASK.md gives, at the place TASK.md names, generated by `tools/make-exit.mjs`, and check it parses. Suggested `aiHub` values: type `Game`, genre `RPG`, source `Diablo 3`, series `Diablo`, players `1–4`, controls `Stick or mouse to move, face buttons or 1-4 for skills, L1 or Q for potion`, tags `3d`, `co-op`, `fantasy`, `boss fights`, `top-down`, `story`. `name` is your title. Suggested tagline: `Seven tolls, and the sun forgets the way`. Suggested description: `An inked co-op action-RPG: cut through candle-headed dead and a tax-collecting devil lord to silence a black bell before the seventh toll.` Use the same tagline in the page `<title>`. Answers to the feedback questions come at the very end, and then you rebuild once more so the screen has them.\n\n**Package:** run `node tools/build.mjs`, copy `dist/game.html` to the single HTML name and location your TASK.md requires, run the whole test suite against that final copy.\n\n**Done means:**\n- [ ] Every row of §22 is true.\n- [ ] Full test suite green against the final file. Whole-campaign bot passes in every class.\n- [ ] Hub harness passes on all scenarios with no warnings.\n- [ ] `grep` of `src/` finds no TODO, FIXME, stub or placeholder.\n- [ ] You looked at screenshots of every zone and screen at 1920×1080.\n- [ ] About/Credits, the exit interview JSON and your chat reply all agree.\n- [ ] Your temporary files are gone and all your processes are stopped.\n\n---\n\n## 22. Brief coverage\n\n| TASK.md asks for | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Source, original game, world, characters, themes, tone | §1, §2, §11 |\n| Genre and perspective choice | §1 |\n| Title: riff, 50 ideas, real RNG | Top of plan, §20 M0 |\n| Research (your choice) | Planner research is reflected here. Report your own in Source Information |\n| Single HTML, CDN optional | §3.1, §21 |\n| Three.js R180, WebGPU, cel/ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API | §3, §12, §14, §5 |\n| Art direction: engine base, new art for source feel | §12 |\n| Animation: engine system, new animations | §13 |\n| Audio: code only, gibberish voices, music 10% | §14 |\n| Online via AI Hub, in the hub and on its own | §18 |\n| Dev folder, modules, bundle, shared-machine rules | §4.1, §19.1, §21 |\n| Performance budget unlimited, no FPS or optimization work | §12 |\n| Testing: headless, whole-game script, one quiet command, no review subagents | §19 |\n| Effort: yours to spend | Spend it where the pillars in §1 say it shows |\n| Feature-complete, long enough, polished slice, infrastructure for designers | §1, §4.3, §20 |\n| Dev mode from Pause, live sliders, reset | §17 |\n| Attract at 10 s, looping, any input exits, may cheat | §16 |\n| Narrative tone like the source | §11 |\n| 10-foot, DualSense first, native keys and mouse, hover focus, last-input prompts, PlayStation and Xbox glyphs | §5, §15 |\n| No dense web-style screens | §15 |\n| Touch-only notice, settings button, attract runs | §15, §16, §3.7 |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §1, §19.4, §20, §21 |\n| Source Information, feedback in chat and About/Credits | §21 |\n| Exit interview JSON | §21 |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: verified recipes\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1035,"totalLines":1271}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TUh2QZULwCWyP7wH1Kyww1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
